      "id": "r1jm0s0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Disease"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Diseases are broadly classified into communicable (infectious) and non-communicable (non-infectious) types.",
        "Deficiency diseases occur due to a lack of essential vitamins, minerals, or nutrients in the diet.",
        "The immune system protects the host from pathogens using innate and acquired defense mechanisms.",
        "Vaccination induces active acquired immunity by training the immune system to recognize specific antigens.",
        "Effective prevention involves personal hygiene, sanitation, vector management, and timely immunization."
      ],
      "id": "749v4ct"
    },
