      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Competitive exams frequently test the differences between innate immunity (present at birth) and acquired immunity (developed after exposure).",
        "Memorize specific nutrient deficiencies and their resulting clinical conditions (e.g., Vitamin A - Night Blindness, Vitamin C - Scurvy, Vitamin D - Rickets).",
        "Understand the primary pathogens (bacteria, virus, protozoa) responsible for major communicable diseases like Tuberculosis, Malaria, and Dengue."
